WEBVTT

00:12.120 --> 00:13.200
Nene?

00:13.730 --> 00:15.490
She has a tail!

00:15.490 --> 00:16.480
And cat ears...

00:16.810 --> 00:18.490
She's a friend's daughter.

00:18.490 --> 00:21.530
She took a joke a bit
too far in her homeland,

00:21.530 --> 00:24.740
so I took her in and helped
her turn things around.

00:24.740 --> 00:26.610
Well, how about that...

00:26.890 --> 00:28.770
Nene, introduce yourself.

00:30.870 --> 00:32.790
I'm Nene Shilfindle.

00:32.790 --> 00:33.000
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

00:33.000 --> 00:34.490
(Ferci Nene)
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

00:34.490 --> 00:34.500
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

00:34.500 --> 00:35.210
(Thief)
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

00:35.210 --> 00:35.970
(Ninja)
I'm a Ferci, formerly a thief, now a ninja.

00:35.970 --> 00:36.880
(Ninja)
I'm rank C!

00:36.880 --> 00:37.750
(Score: Rank C)
I'm rank C!

00:37.750 --> 00:40.290
I'll devote my whole body
and soul to this job!

00:40.930 --> 00:42.880
I promise I'll be useful,

00:43.360 --> 00:45.010
so please hire me!

00:53.140 --> 01:00.110
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:14.970 --> 02:18.520
(Finis Adventurer's Guild)

02:18.980 --> 02:21.980
(Underground Cavern)

02:21.980 --> 02:24.850
(Episode 6: Achromatic Darkness)

02:24.850 --> 02:27.180
(Episode 6: Achromatic Darkness)
I never would have guessed
there'd be an entrance to

02:27.180 --> 02:29.640
Achromatic Darkness beneath
the Adventurer's Guild.

02:29.640 --> 02:31.490
Yeah, I had no idea!

02:31.910 --> 02:34.280
It was right under our feet.

02:34.280 --> 02:35.490
I can't believe it!

02:41.000 --> 02:43.830
The Adventurer's Guild was built
on top of Achromatic Darkness

02:43.830 --> 02:46.250
in order to seal its entrance.

02:46.570 --> 02:48.130
So that's why!

02:49.880 --> 02:53.140
Now, there is something of
which I must inform you.

02:53.880 --> 02:55.310
Ready, Yuke?

02:55.310 --> 02:56.140
Sure.

02:56.640 --> 03:00.060
Of the three A-rank parties
carrying out the investigation,

03:00.060 --> 03:02.980
I'm sure you knew that Scordia backed out,

03:02.980 --> 03:06.150
but just yesterday,
Grant's Blow did the same.

03:06.530 --> 03:09.080
That was quicker than I expected.

03:09.080 --> 03:14.240
Grant's Blow was only in it for the
recognition, anyway. No surprise.

03:14.740 --> 03:19.430
That means Thunder Pike is the
only party in there right now.

03:19.430 --> 03:21.250
And as for Thunder Pike...

03:21.610 --> 03:25.720
Some have alleged that Simon Berkley
has not been transparent as to

03:25.720 --> 03:28.170
how he's spending his sponsorship money.

03:28.170 --> 03:30.880
We have already begun to investigate.

03:31.530 --> 03:33.890
What the hell is he trying to pull?

03:34.420 --> 03:39.020
Otherwise, I only ask that you respect the
established practices for dungeon work.

03:40.120 --> 03:43.900
Which should be obvious, but it's
still the most important thing.

03:45.050 --> 03:47.650
We need to stay alert and be careful.

03:48.020 --> 03:51.020
Prepare several plans in advance.

03:51.650 --> 03:54.410
Rest after every floor.

03:54.410 --> 03:57.640
Check our gains and losses frequently.

03:57.640 --> 04:00.040
And nothing takes higher
priority than our lives.

04:00.640 --> 04:03.460
Okay. Let's have fun, but be careful.

04:13.960 --> 04:16.300
Benwood, Mamar, we'll see you later.

04:16.840 --> 04:19.570
Remember, you're just taking
a quick look around.

04:19.570 --> 04:23.250
No need to go too hard
or bring back souvenirs.

04:23.250 --> 04:24.560
We'll remember.

04:25.100 --> 04:26.690
Take care.

04:27.130 --> 04:28.580
Begin livestream.

04:28.580 --> 04:30.900
Beginning stream.

04:33.260 --> 04:35.120
Hey, it's Clover.

04:35.570 --> 04:37.700
Hope they're gonna put on
another good show today.

04:38.380 --> 04:42.600
This is Clover. We're here today to
investigate Achromatic Darkness.

04:42.600 --> 04:46.210
It's the first day of our
first attempt. Wish us luck!

04:49.710 --> 04:50.680
Let's go.

04:53.210 --> 04:56.720
(Achromatic Darkness, First Floor)

05:11.800 --> 05:13.540
No sign of any enemies.

05:15.740 --> 05:17.980
The wind's blowing from this way.

05:17.980 --> 05:19.240
I'll go scout it out!

05:21.010 --> 05:24.000
Rain, that new staff looks really cool.

05:24.570 --> 05:27.250
Yeah. My Crimson Staff.

05:27.250 --> 05:30.140
It boosts the strength
of my offensive magic.

05:30.140 --> 05:31.500
It feels great in my hands.

05:33.560 --> 05:36.010
So what do you think of
Achromatic Darkness, Master?

05:37.110 --> 05:40.010
I don't feel as emotional
as I thought I would.

05:40.010 --> 05:42.520
Well, we only just got here.

05:43.300 --> 05:46.000
I'm quite excited myself.

05:46.000 --> 05:47.020
Really?

05:48.180 --> 05:50.220
It's embarrassing to admit,

05:50.220 --> 05:52.920
but the reason I decided
to be an adventurer

05:52.920 --> 05:56.150
was to obtain the means to
get by in human society.

05:56.150 --> 05:57.530
In other words, for money.

05:57.930 --> 06:01.030
I don't think that's anything
to be embarrassed about.

06:01.670 --> 06:07.290
What you said that day had
a tremendous effect on me.

06:08.050 --> 06:11.790
I had never even thought about
adventuring to fulfill a dream.

06:11.790 --> 06:17.360
So being here with you in the place you
dreamed about makes my heart race.

06:17.360 --> 06:18.800
Is that childish of me?

06:19.890 --> 06:22.550
It's starting to come back to me now.

06:22.550 --> 06:24.870
It's just ahead of us now, isn't it?

06:24.870 --> 06:27.880
The edge of the world—the Abyss Gate.

06:29.060 --> 06:31.250
I've confirmed our route!

06:31.840 --> 06:35.570
You know... this place is really weird.

06:43.680 --> 06:47.330
I see. This sure is something, all right.

06:49.640 --> 06:52.010
Thunder Pike, the party
that entered before us,

06:52.010 --> 06:55.090
has made it as far as the
eighth floor so far.

06:55.090 --> 06:56.920
The eighth floor?

06:56.920 --> 06:58.450
But it's already been two weeks.

06:58.450 --> 06:59.840
They haven't gotten far at all.

07:00.180 --> 07:01.400
I know.

07:06.450 --> 07:11.130
Our only objective is to find out if there's
anything odd going on in this dungeon.

07:11.130 --> 07:12.850
We're not trying to clear it.

07:13.410 --> 07:16.360
We'll livestream everything as we go,

07:16.730 --> 07:21.110
and the footage will be checked by the
guild master and Royal Academy scholars.

07:21.850 --> 07:23.900
Incidentally, according to said scholars,

07:23.900 --> 07:27.370
this dungeon is an underground tower.

07:27.370 --> 07:28.450
A tower?

07:29.040 --> 07:31.830
Apparently, there are signs
of a stairway leading up.

07:32.680 --> 07:35.910
The logs say that if you try
to force your way to the top,

07:35.910 --> 07:40.880
you'll experience unnecessary losses,
like with the atrium in Aion.

07:40.880 --> 07:46.650
I see. So whether we want to go up
or down, we have to use the stairs.

07:46.650 --> 07:49.640
And that's this dungeon's rule, correct?

07:49.640 --> 07:51.390
Exactly.

07:53.940 --> 07:56.160
There's a monster.

07:56.160 --> 07:58.120
And there's no way around it,

07:58.120 --> 08:00.030
so it looks like we'll have to fight.

08:07.060 --> 08:08.530
I've never seen one of those.

08:08.530 --> 08:11.040
Maybe it's a type of Chimera?

08:11.410 --> 08:14.240
Rain, use a compact offensive spell.

08:14.240 --> 08:15.040
Right.

08:15.640 --> 08:17.290
Silk, attack with your bow.

08:17.590 --> 08:19.440
Target its head if you can.

08:20.220 --> 08:20.800
Right.

08:21.180 --> 08:23.670
And Marina, use this.

08:23.670 --> 08:26.840
Huh? I'm not attacking with a sword?

08:27.210 --> 08:32.100
I want to take it out quickly, before
it can swing that huge axe around.

08:32.100 --> 08:33.810
That makes sense.

08:33.810 --> 08:38.360
This works too, but since that
Memorandum of Revelation you repaired

08:38.360 --> 08:42.530
got me a second job as a Samurai,
I wanted to fight with a sword.

08:42.530 --> 08:45.480
You'll have plenty of chances for that.

08:45.480 --> 08:46.780
Fair enough!

08:47.240 --> 08:51.740
It's amazing that you have the
aptitude for two rare jobs, Marina!

08:51.740 --> 08:55.880
I was hoping I could learn to
use magic, in all honesty.

08:55.880 --> 08:58.090
That's being a bit greedy.

08:58.090 --> 08:59.250
Yeah, I know.

08:59.560 --> 09:00.820
Okay, let's do it.

09:00.820 --> 09:01.500
Right.

09:02.010 --> 09:05.510
Flames, become a magic spear that
houses the fires of purgatory...

09:05.510 --> 09:09.760
With the mingling of black and
white, souls vanish into chaos!

09:10.320 --> 09:12.770
I'll provide support
with my ninjutsu, too!

09:16.390 --> 09:19.150
Prismatic Missile!

09:23.320 --> 09:25.400
Have a taste of this!

09:33.790 --> 09:36.910
Stab and impale! Flame Javelin!

09:57.470 --> 09:59.310
Okay, it's down.

09:59.750 --> 10:01.560
I didn't even get to do anything!

10:01.560 --> 10:05.070
That spell was the same one you
fired at the Zarnag, wasn't it?

10:05.070 --> 10:08.520
And I got to see it!
I got to see it in person!

10:10.460 --> 10:13.920
Looks like this is the safety
area mentioned in the paperwork.

10:13.920 --> 10:15.780
Let's take a break here.

10:15.780 --> 10:16.830
Cut the stream.

10:17.320 --> 10:19.330
Resting. Sleep mode.

10:20.740 --> 10:22.700
Being streamed all the
time is kinda exhausting.

10:22.700 --> 10:24.800
It's like I'm nervous forever.

10:26.020 --> 10:28.090
It's going well so far.

10:28.090 --> 10:29.630
Okay, everyone, anything lost?

10:30.020 --> 10:34.670
I used one arrow with Stinger Joe.

10:34.670 --> 10:36.290
Nothing is lost here.

10:36.290 --> 10:39.160
I used three Attribute Arrows.

10:39.160 --> 10:43.440
I have plenty of extra arrows in
the Magic Bag you bought for me.

10:43.830 --> 10:46.190
My mana's recovered already.

10:46.480 --> 10:48.030
No problems here!

10:48.030 --> 10:50.950
Good. The only question left
is what to do with this.

10:55.450 --> 10:56.990
We're not gonna open it?

10:56.990 --> 10:58.450
Oh, we're opening it.

10:58.450 --> 11:01.830
I'm just not sure whether
we should stream it or not.

11:02.280 --> 11:08.590
If a C-rank party on a special quest
got their hands on a rare artifact...

11:09.220 --> 11:11.590
It might upset some people.

11:11.590 --> 11:12.220
Nene.

11:12.220 --> 11:13.770
Roger!

11:13.770 --> 11:16.130
No streaming this, then.

11:18.450 --> 11:21.980
It's rigged with a trap...
but that's not a problem.

11:23.330 --> 11:26.480
Trap released. And it's unlocked!

11:29.270 --> 11:30.690
Jewels!

11:30.690 --> 11:32.740
This one's a winner!

11:33.070 --> 11:34.490
Any artifacts?

11:35.080 --> 11:38.710
Silk, you hold on to the
jewels and gold for now.

11:38.710 --> 11:39.970
All right.

11:44.280 --> 11:46.050
I'll inspect the rest.

11:47.560 --> 11:51.630
Oh, this is good. It's pretty valuable.

11:56.520 --> 11:57.680
Yuke?

11:57.680 --> 11:59.390
What's that?

11:59.800 --> 12:00.890
I'm not sure.

12:00.890 --> 12:02.640
You're not sure?

12:03.210 --> 12:05.900
I can tell it's an artifact, but...

12:06.640 --> 12:10.400
A box? It's very strange.

12:10.400 --> 12:12.190
If I had to say...

12:12.190 --> 12:14.480
it's like it doesn't know what it is.

12:15.230 --> 12:17.900
Like it's waiting for an answer.

12:17.900 --> 12:20.040
I don't get it.

12:22.100 --> 12:25.040
It's basically like a baby.

12:25.040 --> 12:28.120
What? It's a baby artifact?

12:28.120 --> 12:29.040
I want it!

12:29.040 --> 12:31.300
Yeah. I want it, too.

12:31.640 --> 12:34.390
At any rate, it's rare,

12:34.390 --> 12:36.500
so we'll report it to Benwood first.

12:37.000 --> 12:39.310
It might be a clue that
points us to an abnormality.

12:39.980 --> 12:41.500
Rain, give me your hand.

12:46.230 --> 12:48.540
Looks like your ring finger
is just the right size.

12:56.500 --> 12:58.950
You should be the one to use this ring.

12:59.250 --> 13:00.820
It's called a Sanity Ring.

13:00.820 --> 13:03.930
It has the power to stabilize the mind.

13:03.930 --> 13:04.960
What is it?

13:04.960 --> 13:07.680
Marina can have the box...

13:07.680 --> 13:09.460
Really?! Sweet!

13:21.130 --> 13:23.970
I found the stairs to the second floor!

13:24.440 --> 13:27.480
We're moving at a good pace.
All's going well.

13:27.480 --> 13:28.480
Thanks, Nene.

13:28.480 --> 13:32.120
Nah, it was all thanks to this artifact.

13:32.120 --> 13:36.110
It shows me where stairways and exits
are by detecting wind currents.

13:36.560 --> 13:41.120
I know Wind Priming is an item often used
when exploring new dungeons, but...

13:41.400 --> 13:46.250
You've used so many rare artifacts
that you've become numb to them.

13:46.710 --> 13:48.250
R-Really?

13:53.750 --> 13:58.510
Well, after coming this far, what would you
say seems off about Achromatic Darkness?

13:58.510 --> 14:02.430
Maybe it's how the scenery is
always changing in certain areas?

14:02.430 --> 14:05.640
I think that shark-headed
monster was pretty abnormal.

14:05.980 --> 14:10.920
True. We took out several
monsters on our way here,

14:10.920 --> 14:14.400
but that shark-headed one was special.

14:14.840 --> 14:21.410
So I guess the keys are the shark-headed
monster and the chest that weren't in the logs.

14:23.180 --> 14:26.080
The encounter with a monster that
was out of place on its floor

14:26.080 --> 14:29.540
and the chest we found at the same
time might warrant suspicion.

14:29.860 --> 14:31.420
Um...

14:31.730 --> 14:37.920
A chest appearing in the safety room on the
first floor is pretty abnormal, isn't it?

14:38.790 --> 14:39.870
That's true.

14:39.870 --> 14:44.840
Most treasures you find, like the
strength of the monsters you encounter,

14:44.840 --> 14:47.180
are proportionate to the
risk level of each floor.

14:47.960 --> 14:50.890
But a chest that immediately
gave us a high-quality artifact

14:50.890 --> 14:54.220
and an artifact we couldn't identify...

14:54.220 --> 14:56.190
Was it the right fit for the floor?

14:56.190 --> 14:58.620
So what shall we do?

14:58.620 --> 15:01.470
Well, it's still only the first day.

15:01.470 --> 15:03.070
Let's head back for now.

15:09.600 --> 15:11.080
We're almost at the exit.

15:11.350 --> 15:14.190
Good. We made it back safely.

15:14.190 --> 15:15.590
Good job, everyone.

15:17.120 --> 15:18.840
Someone's close by!

15:19.090 --> 15:20.180
Yuke.

15:24.760 --> 15:28.460
I almost forgot you guys
were down here, too.

15:28.460 --> 15:29.730
These guys...

15:30.020 --> 15:31.890
So that's Thunder Pike?

15:31.890 --> 15:34.730
Yeah. Yuke's former party.

15:36.350 --> 15:39.240
Yuke, if you were coming down here anyway,

15:39.240 --> 15:41.860
why didn't you agree to our request?

15:42.140 --> 15:45.680
Request? That was just
a headhunting scheme.

15:45.680 --> 15:48.870
We've been sent here by the
kingdom on a formal mission.

15:48.870 --> 15:50.250
Yuke...

15:50.540 --> 15:52.750
You'd better start taking us seriously!

15:52.750 --> 15:54.540
I hope you're sorry!

15:54.540 --> 15:57.750
You are severely lacking in gratitude!

16:01.400 --> 16:05.640
Oh, it's fine. We're partners
on the same job now, after all.

16:06.060 --> 16:10.140
Now, give me your streaming data
and everything you've found.

16:10.610 --> 16:14.140
Thunder Pike and Clover
are an alliance now,

16:14.140 --> 16:15.900
so it makes sense to share, right?

16:16.490 --> 16:17.860
What's an alliance?

16:18.470 --> 16:22.990
It's when multiple parties work
together to conquer a dungeon.

16:23.530 --> 16:25.740
I don't recall
forming an alliance with you.

16:26.130 --> 16:29.940
We're offering to ally with
a C-rank party like you.

16:29.940 --> 16:31.250
Be grateful.

16:31.660 --> 16:33.710
You need to thank us this time.

16:33.710 --> 16:36.380
Work well to repent for your actions.

16:39.720 --> 16:41.010
Hey, check it out.

16:41.010 --> 16:42.760
Are they arguing over something?

16:43.200 --> 16:48.260
It'd be more efficient for an A-rank
party like us to make the report, right?

16:48.260 --> 16:49.760
So hand 'em over.

16:51.270 --> 16:52.770
Be serious!

16:54.190 --> 16:55.970
Even if you're an A-rank party,

16:55.970 --> 16:58.770
do you feel no shame in
blackmailing people?!

16:59.070 --> 17:03.770
Whoa, now. A dark elf savage is
in no place to get sassy with us.

17:04.390 --> 17:08.780
Watch your tongue, filthy
follower of a wicked god!

17:08.780 --> 17:10.370
Hey, you guys!

17:10.370 --> 17:11.740
That was rude!

17:11.740 --> 17:14.190
I'm talking to Yuke right now.

17:14.190 --> 17:16.000
Stay out of this, you savage.

17:16.000 --> 17:17.120
Shut up!

17:20.630 --> 17:23.460
Silk is family to me!

17:23.460 --> 17:24.480
Don't you insult her!

17:24.480 --> 17:25.510
Master...

17:25.510 --> 17:29.010
Hey, come on, Yuke. What're
you all worked up about?

17:31.060 --> 17:32.620
Beat it, Simon!

17:32.620 --> 17:33.640
An alliance?

17:34.060 --> 17:36.390
The idea of partnering up
with you guys makes me sick!

17:37.640 --> 17:39.010
You little...

17:39.010 --> 17:40.150
Insolent!

17:41.650 --> 17:42.840
Listen to me.

17:43.370 --> 17:45.650
I will never work with you people.

17:46.490 --> 17:47.530
Yuke...

17:48.090 --> 17:49.600
Let's go, guys.

17:56.040 --> 17:58.380
Uh, that wasn't good, was it?

17:58.380 --> 18:02.590
Yeah, this'll be a problem. A big one.

18:02.590 --> 18:05.340
(Two Days Later)

18:06.590 --> 18:09.590
Allegations have been raised
against Thunder Pike.

18:09.590 --> 18:11.970
Allegations? Against us?

18:13.100 --> 18:16.260
This was jointly signed by your sponsors.

18:16.900 --> 18:19.170
This is from the
Elf Correspondence Council.

18:19.170 --> 18:21.110
This is from the Welmelia
Civil Rights Union.

18:21.110 --> 18:24.860
And this last one is from
guild headquarters.

18:25.550 --> 18:28.110
You know the reason behind
all these, don't you?

18:28.740 --> 18:31.370
If you saw the stream,
you should understand.

18:31.370 --> 18:34.880
In fact, I'd say a C-rank
party insulting us,

18:34.880 --> 18:37.870
an A-rank party, is a much bigger problem.

18:39.120 --> 18:42.580
They were the ones who acted rude first.

18:42.580 --> 18:44.250
I mean, a savage like that dark elf—

18:51.420 --> 18:52.760
Wh-What was—

18:52.760 --> 18:58.020
You seem to have no understanding
whatsoever as to what you've done!

18:58.020 --> 19:01.600
Why should a party that pals around
with a dark elf savage be—

19:06.950 --> 19:10.730
An A-rank adventurer recognized
by the Kingdom of Welmelia

19:10.730 --> 19:13.810
was caught making discriminatory
comments on a livestream.

19:13.810 --> 19:17.040
You people have sullied
the kingdom's dignity.

19:17.040 --> 19:18.890
That's an overreaction!

19:18.890 --> 19:21.670
It was just a little quarrel
between adventurers!

19:24.110 --> 19:25.740
Just a quarrel?

19:25.740 --> 19:29.750
This may damage the kingdom's
relationship with the elves!

19:29.750 --> 19:31.180
Don't be so dramatic!

19:31.710 --> 19:35.750
The members of Thunder Pike will
conduct an apology stream.

19:35.750 --> 19:38.810
You'd best be prepared to forfeit your
adventurer qualifications, as well.

19:39.280 --> 19:42.560
Depending on the ruling,
you may even be exiled.

19:42.560 --> 19:44.310
That's ridiculous!

19:44.310 --> 19:46.360
You're the ridiculous ones here!

19:49.130 --> 19:50.910
What about the mission?

19:50.910 --> 19:53.490
You'd be up a creek without us, you know!

19:55.240 --> 19:59.420
If that C-rank party is the only one
left to take on Achromatic Darkness,

19:59.420 --> 20:00.850
won't that cause problems?

20:00.850 --> 20:04.620
We applied, got approval,
and the seal was lifted.

20:04.620 --> 20:07.490
In other words, without an
A-rank party like us—

20:07.490 --> 20:09.420
It won't cause any problems at all.

20:09.420 --> 20:14.680
Unlike you half-wits,
Clover has achieved a great deal.

20:16.470 --> 20:19.080
So long as they are
undertaking this mission,

20:19.080 --> 20:23.200
Clover is provisionally
registered as an A-rank party.

20:23.200 --> 20:24.600
There's no problem at all.

20:24.860 --> 20:26.790
What?!

20:26.790 --> 20:28.730
Those guys... are A-rank?!

20:29.000 --> 20:34.490
Reflect on what you've done and
come up with an apology to stream.

20:41.640 --> 20:45.830
Apologize? Why should I have to do that?!

20:47.640 --> 20:51.290
Damn that Yuke! He set us
up with that stream of his!

20:51.290 --> 20:53.130
He's gonna pay for that!

20:53.130 --> 20:54.840
Simon?

20:57.840 --> 21:00.750
No need to be so wary of me.

21:00.750 --> 21:06.230
Well? Don't you want to get back
at Yuke Feldio and Clover?

21:08.500 --> 21:10.710
I have a great idea.

21:10.710 --> 21:15.240
You get to be on top again,
and I get what I want.

21:15.240 --> 21:16.680
What do you say?

21:18.060 --> 21:20.350
How about you tell me more?

22:56.000 --> 22:56.600
(The Pale, Immortal Ruler)

22:56.600 --> 22:59.540
(The Pale, Immortal Ruler)
Next time, "The Pale, Immortal Ruler."

22:59.540 --> 23:01.010
(The Pale, Immortal Ruler)
